{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/912420-how-rituals-actually-work","id":912420,"title":"How rituals actually work","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-11T13:59:17-07:00","id":912420,"title":"How rituals actually work","content":"I admit I don't get the metaphysical explanation about rituals in Second Edition . Are they supposed to be a shortcut to directly summoning a spirit and bargain for a favor, based on previous interactions and agreements between the People and the different Chorus? is the essence generated by the ritual the payment to such spirits, or may they demand something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-11-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:20:27-07:00","id":912430,"title":"","content":"The Shadow has a metaphysical framework that steers interactions between spirits and resonance and the Gauntlet and all of those other little variables that the Ithaeur learn about.<br /> <br /> Rites play into that framework with symbolism filtered through the totem bond and/or the nature of werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:46:24-07:00","id":912452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/912420-how-rituals-actually-work?p=912430#post912430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow has a metaphysical framework that steers interactions between spirits and resonance and the Gauntlet and all of those other little variables that the Ithaeur learn about.<br /> <br /> Rites play into that framework with symbolism filtered through the totem bond and/or the nature of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't quite understand. Could you clarify, maybe with an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:16:33-07:00","id":912477,"title":"","content":"I don't know about an example, but to clarify a bit of what I think Satchel is saying, in Chronicles of Darkness, symbols have power. It's a major recurring theme across several lines that symbols aren't just reflections of reality, reality is also a reflection of symbols. Many forms of magic in Chronicles of Darkness, including most spirit magic, works on the same principles. You manipulate symbols to depict a desired outcome, and imbue that act with some kind of metaphysical energy (Willpower, Mana, Essence, etc.), and reality conforms to the symbolism you create. Rites are just another example of this - in this case, you are doing so according to certain metaphysical laws of the Shadow, utilizing the symbolic power of the totemic bond, and the dual spirit/flesh nature of werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-11-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:41:34-07:00","id":912487,"title":"","content":"Why does a hunger spirit seek out hunger essence? Why does a spirit merely gain in Rank when consuming one type of essence, but become a magath when consuming a different type? Why do spirits arrange themselves into families and choruses and courts? Because that's how the Shadow works. That's not <i>all</i> of what the Shadow is, but it gives you a sense of the kind of spiritual law that dominates the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Rites, essentially, are built off an intuitive understanding of that law and exploit it in order to achieve effects. There's no explicit encoding of that law; you get to make that up for your table, to the extent that you care. But you can scrape it together by basically having a vague understanding of what makes the Shadow tick, its themes and tropes and symbols, and picking elements for the rite that feel like they'd fit into those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:51:14-07:00","id":912493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/912420-how-rituals-actually-work?p=912452#post912452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't quite understand. Could you clarify, maybe with an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're calling on the laws of the Shadow \u2014 a crowded patchwork quilt of resonance wherein basically everything is potentially sentient and has some degree of sway over the material world \u2014 to accomplish an effect through the invocation of symbolic resonance with the desired process and/or outcome.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, yes, it's kind of a shortcut to bargaining for a favor. On the other hand, many of the effects rites provide are outside the scope of most spirits that aren't at least <i>Dihim</i> and those things generally have powers that set precedents for rites in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:22:31-07:00","id":912578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/912420-how-rituals-actually-work?p=912493#post912493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, yes, it's kind of a shortcut to bargaining for a favor. On the other hand, many of the effects rites provide are outside the scope of most spirits that aren't at least <i>Dihim</i> and those things generally have powers that set precedents for rites in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of fact, several Rites were literally created by binding powerful spirits to eternal promises.<br /> <br /> The Shadow has laws that can be exploited by the ones who manage to understand those laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T23:59:26-07:00","id":912675,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks to everyone for your thoughts of the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-12-2016, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}